        "id": "ingres-gw-assessment-tn",
        "title": "IN-GRES dynamic groundwater assessment (Chennai-area blocks)",
        "publisher": "CGWB / IIT-Hyderabad (IN-GRES)",
        "license": "no explicit licence: the IN-GRES portal publishes no terms of use, no disclaimer and no copyright or licence statement anywhere; nothing has been established about who may redistribute this material or on what terms"
      }
    ],
    "method": "api",
    "produced_at": "2026-10-05",
    "produced_by": "neer-vazhvu-api/scripts/build_ingres_gwr.py",
    "note": "Block-level dynamic groundwater assessment (category and stage of extraction) for Chennai district's 16 taluk assessment units. 2011 to 2020 come from the WRIS NWIC GWR{year}_CGWB ArcGIS services (scripts/fetch-wris-groundwater.ts); 2022-23 onward from the IN-GRES API, upserted in place by build_ingres_gwr.py --city chennai, which reproduces the WRIS 2023 and 2024 vintages to 0.1 ham. IN-GRES units are matched by assessed area, not by name: in the 2022-23, 2023-24 and 2024-25 editions IN-GRES prints Chennai's taluk names one place out of step with their areas from Madhavaram on (the 7,068 ha Sholinganallur unit is labelled Purasaivakkam), and 2025-26 prints the same areas under their true names. The 2025-26 edition is not included: it assesses 17 units, and these 16 polygons are the earlier set.",
    "conventions": {
      "comparability": "CGWB assessment units can change between GEC editions (block/firka/village granularity shifts); year-on-year comparisons must check assessment-unit continuity before differencing. Chennai's units were redrawn for 2025-26: Kolathur (700 ha) is carved out of Ayanavaram (1,529 to 829 ha) and Thiruvottiyur is 285 ha smaller."
    }
  },
  "source": "CGWB assessment, via India WRIS (to 2020) and IN-GRES (from 2022-23)",
